Release DLL AdaptivePapyrusBudget 0.3.0 run through its real entry path (Plugin.cpp: INI reading,
menu/load gate, periodic report), 2026-11-10 08:46-09:00.

Build under test: source after the 2026-11-10 review fixes (queue-front check before a cycle, new
counters, violation stop, collecting only while engaged, strict INI switches, locale-independent
numbers). DLL SHA-256 D5029BA57757B9A876E5EFD434CF3CAB67C38236973A2E8FD74829BCBECE4575.
This is not the DLL in dist/AdaptivePapyrusBudget-0.3.0-AE1170.zip (25429bd8...), which predates
those fixes and has never been run in the game.

Setup: profile APB-CatchUp-Release, Save93 loaded by APBTestSaveLoader, SSE Display Tweaks limiter
30 FPS, DynamicUpdateBudget off, Papyrus log off, Papyrus Tweaks NG 4.1.1 active (iMaxOpsPerFrame
500, bSpeedUpNativeCalls off). The profile lists TulliusNovelistProbe-0.0.3 as enabled, but that
mod folder no longer exists, so it was not loaded. The player stands still in Whiterun; no menu
was opened and no save was made, so the menu gate and the save freeze were not exercised. The game
window was not kept in front (the user worked over a remote session), so frame-cost numbers below
are not measurements. Script: build/catchup/run-release-check.ps1; run folders relcheck-off,
relcheck-carried, relcheck-accelerate.

Result summary
- Mode=off with [General] Enabled=flase: the typo is reported and the feature stays off; no hook is
  installed; the game ran 90 s after the save load.
- Mode=carried with MaxExtraMS=1.5 and [NativePacing] Enabled=maybe: the number is read as 1.50 ms,
  the typo is reported and native pacing stays off. One full report minute: 1,795 frames, all
  engaged, 148 held after the load, 11 extra cycles that dispatched 174 queued messages, 1,483
  frames skipped because the queue front had to wait, guard_violations 0.
- Mode=accelerate with the packaged INI: two full report minutes. Second minute: 1,800 frames,
  1,185 extra cycles, 3,268 queued messages dispatched (about 2.8 per cycle), 579 frames skipped
  because the front had to wait (32 %), 905 cycles stopped at a waiting front, 15 idle stops,
  guard_violations 0, overrun_pauses 0, at most 0.55 ms extra in a frame.
- leftover_tasklets was 0 (carried), 2 and 4 (accelerate) per minute: in this scene and with the
  500-op limit, tasklets carried over by the op limit are almost absent, so the extra tasklet
  batches ran the scripts the cycle's own calls resumed. The vanilla 100-op limit and busier scenes
  are not covered by this.
- Every run left the two exit crash logs of the known pattern (execution of an unmapped 64 KB
  aligned address while the game closes), after the run had completed.

